  "hypothesis": "On the physical image, increasing outstanding depth from 1 to 8 reduces the resident (a+b)*0.5 graph's launch cycles, while a third active outlet does not help at depth 8, as the RTL stand-in showed (19,132 vs 21,623 cycles); the model ordering is the one to test, not its absolute cycles.",
  "competing_explanations": [
    "physical HBM controller latency differs from the synthetic AXI slave",
    "cache geometry (B40 32/8) changes maintenance traffic relative to the RTL stand-in (4/2)",
    "outlet controls are refused or not applied by the image (checked by readback)",
    "ABI uploads/maintenance inside the native call dominate"
  ],
  "expected_counter_changes": [
    "outlet read/write line deltas split across 1 or 3 outlets as configured; totals unchanged",
    "cycles(1/8) < cycles(1/1); cycles(3/8) not below cycles(1/8) beyond sample spread"
  ],
  "expected_observations": [
    "3 configurations x 3 independent interleaved processes pass numerically with readback-confirmed controls"
  ],
